# Agent configuration. settings.json is committed team policy;
# settings.local.json is personal and must never be. Both of these were
# previously covered only by machine-local git config — a personal global
# gitignore and .git/info/exclude — neither of which travels with a clone,
# so a new contributor had no protection at all.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
